DESCRIPTION:Talk description:\n\nAt the heart of the hit movie\, “The Od
 yssey\,” is director-writer Christopher Nolan’s focus on the Trojan Ho
 rse and the sack of Troy. He contends that it was “a violation of the la
 w of Zeus\,” which today we would call a war crime. But was it a war cri
 me? Would the ancient Greeks have considered it a crime? And what would th
 e law of armed conflict say if the Trojan Horse episode took place today? 
 Strauss discusses these questions in a talk that represents work in progre
 ss on his\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://classics.stanford.edu/events/
 all-upcoming-events\nLast synced: 2026-10-16 10:11 PDT
LOCATION:Building 110
URL:https://classics.stanford.edu/events/all-upcoming-events
