BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[CREEES Center for Russian\, East European & Eurasian Studies / Hi
 story Department] Fate in My Hands: The Death Penalty in the Soviet Union
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T130000
DTSTAMP:20261016T171154Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53851057231744-53851057232769@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Fate in My Hands: The Death Penalty in the Soviet Union docume
 nts in striking\, heart-rending detail how Soviet citizens\, hopeful for a
  new life post-Stalin\, lost faith that their transgressions could be forg
 iven.\n\nFrom 1954 to 1991 in the Soviet Union\, nearly forty thousand cit
 izens were executed after the death penalty was reinstated as a punishment
  for homicide. Fate in My Hands introduces readers to the many citizens in
  this period—women and men of all ages and backgrounds—who found thems
 elve\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-16 10:11 PDT
LOCATION:Encina Hall
END:VEVENT
